# EVERY compact CALL BELOW DECLARES ITS STDIN OR PASSES -f, DELIBERATELY. The arms that
# assert on facts printed before the prompt read `</dev/null` (EOF = decline), and the
# arms that exercise the handover machinery pass `-f` to skip the prompt entirely. Left
# to ambient stdin these hang for a human running the suite from a terminal, and pass or
# fail by whatever the caller happened to supply — an undeclared input is a dependency.
